<div class="page-header">
  <h1 class="page-header__title">Deployment Tools Without the Usual Setup Overhead</h1>
  <p class="page-header__subtitle">
    HelloDeploy brings common deployment tasks into one interface. Configure a supported
    application, deploy it, connect a domain, manage environment variables, review logs, and
    publish updates from one place.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="feature-grid">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'projects' }) %></p>
      <h2 class="feature-title">Deployment management</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Create a project, configure its deployment settings, start a deployment, watch its
        status, and redeploy — all from one dashboard.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'detection' }) %></p>
      <h2 class="feature-title">Build configuration</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Most applications need a build step before they can run in production. HelloDeploy
        inspects a connected repository, suggests a build command for the runtimes it
        recognises, and lets you correct it before the first deployment.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'deploy' }) %></p>
      <h2 class="feature-title">Start commands</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        HelloDeploy needs to know how your application starts once it is built. Set the start
        command and the port the application listens on, and the platform runs it the same way
        on every deployment.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'environment' }) %></p>
      <h2 class="feature-title">Environment variables</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Keep database URLs, API keys, secrets, and service credentials out of your source
        code. Values are encrypted at rest with AES-256-GCM and injected when the container
        starts — never stored in plaintext and never shown in logs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'activity' }) %></p>
      <h2 class="feature-title">Deployment logs</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Follow a deployment as it runs. Logs cover dependency installation, the build,
        application startup, and the health check, so a failure points at the stage that
        actually broke.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'domain' }) %></p>
      <h2 class="feature-title">Project URL</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Every deployed project is reachable at a HelloDeploy address such as
        <code class="code-inline">my-project.<%= deploymentDomain %></code>, with no DNS
        work on your side.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'server' }) %></p>
      <h2 class="feature-title">Custom domains</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Connect a domain you already own. You prove ownership with a TXT record, an
        administrator reviews and provisions the domain, and you point a CNAME at the address
        HelloDeploy shows you. Registering a domain is separate — HelloDeploy does not sell
        domains.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'check' }) %></p>
      <h2 class="feature-title">HTTPS</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Traffic between a visitor's browser and a deployed application is served over HTTPS,
        so page contents and form submissions are encrypted in transit.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'overview' }) %></p>
      <h2 class="feature-title">Redeployment and rollback</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Publish a new version without rebuilding your configuration from scratch. HelloDeploy
        keeps your recent healthy releases, so you can roll back to one if an update goes
        wrong.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'repository' }) %></p>
      <h2 class="feature-title">Deploy hooks</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        A deploy hook is a private URL that starts a deployment when something sends a request
        to it — useful for triggering a release from a script or an external workflow. Treat
        it like a password: anyone holding the URL can deploy your project.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'dashboard' }) %></p>
      <h2 class="feature-title">Project dashboard</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        One place to see current status, the most recent deployment, the project's domains,
        build and runtime settings, environment configuration, logs, and the actions available
        to you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'audit' }) %></p>
      <h2 class="feature-title">Access and audit</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Invite collaborators as Owner, Maintainer, or Viewer, and transfer ownership when a
        project changes hands. Deployments, configuration changes, and access events are
        recorded with the actor and the outcome.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card mt-8">
  <div class="card__body text-center">
    <h2 class="feature-title">See how these features work together</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">
      Follow a deployment from project configuration through build, health check, routing, and
      production updates.
    </p>
    <div class="button-group mt-4">
      <a href="/how-it-works" class="button button--primary">How It Works</a>
      <a href="/auth/create-account" class="button button--secondary">Get Started</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
